  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜ように なりました: coming to be able to",
     "texto": [
      "To say you have come to do something, dictionary-form or potential-form verb + **ように なりました**: **はなせる ように なりました** (I came to be able to speak).",
      "It describes a change that has already happened."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜ように して います: trying to do something",
     "texto": [
      "To say you make an effort to do something as a habit: dictionary-form verb + **ように して います**: **はやく おきる ように して います** (I try to get up early).",
      "It describes an effort that is kept up over time."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜てみる: trying to do",
     "texto": [
      "The て form + **みます** expresses trying something to see how it is: **あたらしい りょうり を たべてみます** (I'll try the new dish). It doesn't simply mean «to see» with the eyes."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
